IMPORT daydate

-- Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation in force from 1 July 2022 -- NOUNS.
--
-- Nouns only: the parties and acts the regulative rules are about, and the records
-- that carry the facts of one employment.  No rules and no directives here.
-- A noun is a fact a witness of ordinary competence could testify to; whether the
-- fact makes a dismissal unlawful, or a dispute a "re-employment dispute", is a rule
-- and lives in the module of the section that says so.

-- The parties of the Act's duties and prohibitions (the regulative rules).
-- There is no party for an official: the Minister, the Commissioner, an investigating
-- officer, a Magistrate and the Employment Claims Tribunal appear only in what they
-- mean for the person in the seat.
DECLARE Party IS ONE OF
    Employer
    Employee
    `A person summoned`
    `Any person`

-- The acts the regulative rules are about, one per duty or prohibition of the Act.
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    `dismiss the employee on the ground of age`
    `give the employee written notice of the intention not to re-employ`
    `offer re-employment`
    `give the employer written notice of the intention to retire`
    `pay the employment assistance payment as a single lump sum`
    `notify the Commissioner in writing of the re-employment dispute`
    `notify the Commissioner in writing of the dismissal`
    `submit a mediation request to the Commissioner`
    `make written representations to the Minister to be re-employed`
    `comply with the direction of the Minister`
    `attend as the summons requires`
    `hinder or obstruct an investigating officer`
    `obstruct an employee in appearing before the Commissioner`

-- The facts of one employment that fix the ages the Act turns on.
-- The prescribed ages are specified by the Minister by notification in the Gazette
-- (ss 4(1) and 7A(11)); the notifications are not among the sources, so they are facts
-- the case supplies.  A retirement age may or may not be stipulated in the contract.
DECLARE Employment HAS
    `date of birth` IS A DATE
    `prescribed minimum retirement age` IS A NUMBER
    `retirement age stipulated in the contract of service` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `prescribed re-employment age` IS A NUMBER

-- A penalty the Act states as a ceiling: "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6
-- months or ... both".  The two figures are the most a court may impose; a sentence actually passed is a fact of the case.
DECLARE Penalty HAS
    `maximum fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `maximum imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER

-- The kinds of factor on which a re-employment contract may vary the job scope and the terms (section 7A(5)).
-- The first four are the factors the section names "such as, but not limited to".
DECLARE `Factor for a variation` IS ONE OF
    `the employee's productivity`
    `the employee's performance`
    `the employee's duties and responsibilities`
    `the wage system, such as the seniority system, applicable to the employee`
    `another factor`

-- The purposes for which service under an earlier contract may or may not be counted (sections 7B and 7C(6)).
DECLARE `Purpose of reckoning service` IS ONE OF
    `computing the minimum period of 3 months for entitlement to annual leave under section 88A(1) of the Employment Act 1968`
    `determining the period of service for entitlement to paid sick leave under section 89(1) and (2) of the Employment Act 1968`
    `determining another right, privilege, obligation or liability under the re-employment contract`

-- The matters over which section 8A(4) says a re-employment dispute can be.
DECLARE `Dispute matter` IS ONE OF
    `denial of re-employment because the employee does not satisfy the eligibility criteria set out in section 7(1)`
    `denial of re-employment, in accordance with section 7C(1), because the employer is unable to find a suitable vacancy`
    `the reasonableness of the terms and conditions of a re-employment offer`
    `the reasonableness of the amount of an employment assistance payment offered`
    `another matter`

-- What the Minister must or may have regard to in fixing compensation (sections 8(4) and 8B(10)).
DECLARE `Consideration in fixing compensation` IS ONE OF
    `the loss sustained by the employee in consequence of the unlawful dismissal`
    `the employee's prospects in obtaining alternative employment`
    `the steps taken by the employee to mitigate his or her loss`
    `the period the employee has served with the employer`
    `the employee's age`
    `the tripartite guidelines`
    `the steps taken by the employer to re-employ the employee`
    `any other consideration`

-- The powers of the Commissioner and of an investigating officer in section 9(1)(a) to (g).
DECLARE `Power under section 9(1)` IS ONE OF
    `enter a place of employment without previous notice to conduct an audit or make an inquiry`
    `examine a person orally`
    `require the employer to produce an employee together with a contract of service or other document`
    `make copies of a document required to be produced`
    `take or remove a document for the purposes of investigations`
    `take photographs or audio or video recordings of the premises and of persons`
    `require a person to produce an article and take it into custody`
    `another power`
